# <project name> local verification environment (real-hardware e2e verification)
#
# Copy to .env and fill in your own real targets; .env is already in .gitignore and will not be
# committed.
# The application itself does not read this file; only the e2e harness loads it into the
# environment during a test run (see <harness config file>, which skips it when absent), for the
# local verification track.
# Purpose, wiring and safety notes are in e2e/README.md, under "Verifying against a real environment".
#
# Reminder: a real target = real side effects (not hermetic), so run only read-only /
# non-destructive operations.
# Smoke e2e never uses this file — that track must be entirely mocked.
#
# One KEY=value per line with no inline comments, so copying it to .env parses trivially.
# Fill in only the services you genuinely have; delete any block you do not need.

# --- <service A> ---
E2E_<A>_HOST=<placeholder address>
E2E_<A>_PORT=<port>
E2E_<A>_USER=<username>
E2E_<A>_PASSWORD=changeme

# --- <service B> ---
# <write this service's particular traps here, e.g.: the private key path must be absolute,
# because ~ is not expanded when read — expand ~ to $HOME yourself>
E2E_<B>_HOST=<placeholder address>
E2E_<B>_PORT=<port>
# Auth method: key | password
E2E_<B>_AUTH=key
E2E_<B>_KEY=<absolute path>
# Only filled in when E2E_<B>_AUTH=password:
# E2E_<B>_PASSWORD=
